#data scaling#
scale.data matrix normalises by gene, after data matrix normalizes by gene expression per cell
!scale.data is very heavy and only run on genes of interest
data1@ gives you all associated layers as options, i.e. data1@assays$RNA@cells

# Data integration #
We normalize and scale data separately - in this case, they do not cluster by sample (at least, do it less)
Ways to integrateSeurat pipeline: SCT transform. Modify/infer underlying data to look for connectivityBidirectional PCA or correlational analysis to create "anchors" between data. Then applying a correction vector to our data.Encouraged by Seurat but not widely accepted by community.
Alternative approaches:
-Liger. Aligns nearest neighbor graph. Similar pairings come into alignment, then used for UMAP Presently incompartible w Seurat cluster :)
- Harmony. Aligning principal components then using them. Alison's go-to.Note: HarmonyTS in Python and Harmony in R are two different packages :)
